From 3576ad627b5ba51066c6520d2fe6164aa21073c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Norris <will@biohack.net>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] [MOS] Legalize and select far pointer values and memory
 accesses

Pass, legalize and select address-space-2 pointers and the byte loads and stores through them.

Calls: a far pointer argument is assigned to RL1-RL3 and its calling-convention type is i32; incoming 32-bit values are accepted. A far pointer that finds no free quad goes to a 4-byte stack slot; it never falls through to the generic pointer rule, whose 16-bit RS pair cannot hold it. Legalization: p2 is legal for G_GLOBAL_VALUE, G_FRAME_INDEX and G_BLOCK_ADDR, converts to and from s32 with G_PTRTOINT/G_INTTOPTR, and takes s32 offsets in G_PTR_ADD, which always use the integer carry chain so the add carries into the bank byte. A p2 G_PHI becomes an s32 PHI, with casts placed before each predecessor's terminator and after the block's PHIs. Casting a near pointer to far zero-extends it (bank $00) without the zero-page bias used for direct-page pointers. A byte load or store through a constant or global far address becomes G_LOAD_FAR_ABS/G_STORE_FAR_ABS (absolute long, `lda $xxxxxx`); through a runtime far pointer it becomes G_LOAD_FAR_INDIR/G_STORE_FAR_INDIR (`lda [dp]`).

Selection: s32 register values use Imag32; a 2 x s16 merge composes an Imag32 with REG_SEQUENCE and an s32 unmerge splits it by word; the far address of a symbol (by address space, including aliases, not by section name) is built from MO_ADDR24_SEG_LO/_SEG_HI/_BANK immediates, which lower to the ADDR24 relocation modifiers; the far access pseudos pin their pointer operand to Imag32 so the cast chain coalesces into the quad `[dp]` reads. Under +mos-a16 the low word of an Imag32 value, as in a far-to-near cast or a truncated ptrtoint, is its sublo16 subregister. Allocation hints skip candidates whose width differs from the copy's other side. MOSLateOptimization's LDImm combining tracks only immediate loads into A, X or Y, and LDCImm treats any nonzero immediate as a set carry.

The 65816 reaches data outside bank DBR only through long addressing; a 16-bit pointer cannot name it. Other MOS CPUs have no long addressing, and the same opcode bytes decode as unrelated instructions there. On those CPUs a far load, store or extending load is therefore diagnosed ("far (address space 2) memory access requires 65816 long addressing; the target CPU has none") instead of being selected. Passing or storing a far pointer as a value stays legal on every CPU.

Default-mode effect: none for code that compiled before: assembly and objects are identical in mos6502 and mosw65816. Five corpus inputs that use address space 2 fail in both default modes before and after this commit, with a different error: without +mos-a16, the s32 merges and unmerges that far pointers need are not legal. On mos6502, three of the five now stop at the far-access diagnostic instead of a legalization error.

Tests: far-addressing.ll checks absolute-long and `[dp]` loads and stores in assembly and object bytes ($af/$8f/$a7/$87), and that a near symbol placed in a far section stays near. far-phi.ll checks the p2 PHI legalization and a `[dp]` load in the emitted loop. far-ptr-arg-exhaustion.ll checks caller and callee with a fourth far pointer, and near/far interleavings that use up the quads while RS1 stays free: the far pointer takes a 4-byte stack slot and never an RS pair (call lowering in plain mosw65816, +mos-a16 and +mos-a16,+mos-xy16; full compilation in the last two). far-access-non-65816.ll checks the diagnostic on mos6502, mos65c02 and mosspc700, that a far pointer can still be passed as a value there, and that the same accesses compile on mosw65816. far-ptr-trunc.ll checks the far-to-near cast and truncated ptrtoint at O0 and O2.

Validate: `build/bin/llvm-lit -v llvm/test/CodeGen/MOS/far-addressing.ll llvm/test/CodeGen/MOS/far-phi.ll llvm/test/CodeGen/MOS/far-ptr-arg-exhaustion.ll llvm/test/CodeGen/MOS/far-access-non-65816.ll llvm/test/CodeGen/MOS/far-ptr-trunc.ll`.

Rebase preparation of the monolithic far-data patch: OpenAI Codex CLI 0.157.1 (session source vscode), model gpt-6-astra, xhigh reasoning effort; verified session 01a0e67f-298f-7a21-80af-06f867085f84. Implementation provenance remains in the source patches and investigations at wbniv/llvm-mos-65816 c3a53aecbc48. Split into this series: Claude Code 2.1.283 (t4-opus-high agent), model Claude Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5), high reasoning effort. Repairs and review follow-ups carried into this commit: Claude Code 2.1.285 (t4-opus-high agent), model Claude Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5), high reasoning effort.

